# tools/m/mycelium_chorus_knot_witness.rish -- a quorum's position survives a checkpoint (r3).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) - Mycelium consensus - the Chorus - rung r3 -- across a Knot.
# r1 gathered a Chorus (a bounded quorum of independent Vouchers for one account position at one
# order-head) believed only when a threshold of distinct nodes agree; r2 let the whole quorum travel. Yet
# a ledger a family runs for years does not carry its whole past unbroken -- the Knot ties off a committed
# prefix into a sealed supply, and the Lapse continues its deadline clock across the seal by carrying the
# epoch base. r3 (mycelium/chorus_knot.rye, mirroring voucher_knot) reads a whole quorum over a ledger
# resolved ACROSS an epoch cut.
#
# The crux this witness proves is A QUORUM'S POSITION SURVIVES A CHECKPOINT: a mesh of distinct nodes
# vouches Alice's position against the whole Cord, and a counterparty who has already checkpointed (sealed
# the prefix into a Knot, discarded the base blocks, continued only the live suffix) reads the identical
# agreed position from that Knot-continued ledger. check_position_across re-runs r1's quorum law at the
# threshold, then confirms the one agreed triple equals the continued ledger's reading. Proven on a pledge
# that lapses across the cut (coins home) and a far-deadline pledge honored in the suffix (received
# accumulates across the base, never restarts). The honest seam: the ORDER-HEAD is the whole-history
# fingerprint (base included), distinct from the prefix-only head in the claim and in every member, so no
# node can silently name a shorter order; a party that pruned the base checks the position, not the head. A
# forged member and a thin threshold each fail the quorum law and match no checkpoint; a corrupt Knot
# refuses whole. Composes chorus + voucher + statement + lapse_knot + lapse + cord + fold + kumara public
# API only; demo seeds -- no key, no funds, no network, no custody.
#
# Scope: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-102533_mycelium-chorus-quorum-attestation-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mycelium_chorus_knot_witness.rish

say "mycelium-chorus-knot: Language EN — a quorum a family gathered years ago still proves a holder's standing to a neighbor who long since checkpointed and threw the old blocks away: the agreed position reads continuous across the seal."
say "mycelium-chorus-knot: Style Radiant — the epoch base keeps the clock and the inflow unbroken, so a mesh's agreed reading does not drift at the checkpoint; a party who kept only the Knot and its live suffix reads the same true position the quorum signed."
say "mycelium-chorus-knot: Lens TAME — check_position_across re-runs the quorum law then confirms the agreed triple against a Knot-continued ledger; the order-head is a whole-history fingerprint base-included; a forged member · a thin threshold · a corrupt Knot each refuse; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/chorus-knot"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/chorus_knot.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-chorus-knot: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-chorus-knot: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "reads true to a party who checkpointed the prefix" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: survives-checkpoint claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "received accumulates across the cut" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: received-accumulates claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "the order-head is the whole-history fingerprint, base included" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: whole-history-head claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "a forged member and a thin threshold each fail the quorum law and match no checkpoint" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: tamper-refusal claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "a quorum's agreed position survives a checkpoint" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: closing claim missing"

# The rendered quorum a keeper reads -- Alice's lapsed position across the cut, vouched by three voices.
assert selftest.out contains "chorus head=" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: rendered quorum missing"
assert selftest.out contains "balance=100 reserved=0 received=100 voices=3" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: rendered lapsed quorum missing"

# The Chorus the checkpoint reads across, and the Lapse-Knot whose base keeps the clock, stand at the door.
let chorus = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/chorus.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/chorus && mycelium/bin/chorus 2>&1"]
assert chorus.ok else "mycelium-chorus-knot: the Chorus read across the cut is not GREEN"
assert chorus.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: the Chorus did not speak its GREEN"

let lapseknot = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/lapse_knot.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/lapse-knot && mycelium/bin/lapse-knot 2>&1"]
assert lapseknot.ok else "mycelium-chorus-knot: the Lapse-Knot whose base keeps the clock is not GREEN"
assert lapseknot.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-chorus-knot: the Lapse-Knot did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-chorus-knot: GREEN — a quorum's agreed position survives a checkpoint, continuous across the epoch base (a pledge that lapses across the cut and a far-deadline pledge honored in the suffix both read true); the order-head is a whole-history fingerprint base included; a forged member · a thin threshold · a corrupt Knot each refuse; the Chorus and the Lapse-Knot stand at the door."
